format: 2
name: a Unicode escape in a line comment is read as javac reads it (T24, fixed)
class: Probe
method: m
arg: 05
expect: AGREE
note: javac translates Unicode escapes before anything else (JLS 21 §3.3), so the escape for a line
note: terminator ends the line comment and the rest of the line is code: the JVM returns 2a. JuLC's
note: parsers left escapes untranslated, so the whole line was a comment and UPLC returned a.
note: Fixed for T24: every parser comes from JavaSourceParser, which translates escapes first. Before
note: the fix the expectation was DIVERGE T24 Value/Value, with JVM Value 0a and UPLC Value 05.
---
import java.math.BigInteger;

public class Probe {
    public static BigInteger m(BigInteger a) {
        return a // \u000a .add(a)
        ;
    }
}
